<title>UK: BA says remains confident of merger approval.</title>
<headline>BA says remains confident of merger approval.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Airways Plc on Friday said it remained confident that its planned alliance with American Airlines would win regulatory approval, after a newspaper report said the plan could ultimately be blocked.</p>
<p>&quot;We remain confident all the relevant approvals will be forthcoming and for the benefit of consumers we hope they will come sooner rather than later,&quot; said a spokesman for the company.</p>
<p>Earlier a report in the Guardian newspaper said the UK government and the European Commission could scupper the planned alliance, saying BA had so far failed to convince Brussels or the Office of Fair Trading that it could meet tough competition criteria.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
